{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.root_of_unity_truncation_conditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.root_of_unity_truncation_conditional","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/root-of-unity-truncation.lean#L63-L83","doc":"**Root-of-unity truncation (conditional).**\n\nConditional on the q-NS conjecture cone and the `q`-Laplacian\nspectral tower, the limit `q → 1` factors through the dense set of\nroots of unity, where each root yields a **finite-rank**\ntruncation: the vortex-core aspect ratio obeys the bounded-degree\nBernstein bound `κ(t) ≤ 1 + C·(κ-1)`, and the boxed equivalence\n\"NS blows up ⟺ `κ(t) = O(1)`\" holds.\n\n*Derived* from the two hypotheses of\n`RootOfUnityTruncationContext` (it composes them; it does not\nassume its own conclusion).\n\nRef: [leitner2026] §Fluid dynamics / Root-of-unity truncation,\n     prop:root-of-unity-truncation ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:root-of-unity-truncation","label":"prop:root-of-unity-truncation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/root-of-unity-truncation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.blowup_iff_coreBounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.blowup_iff_coreBounded","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/root-of-unity-truncation.lean#L61-L61","doc":"**Boxed equivalence (conditional).**  NS blows up at the\ncollision **iff** the core aspect ratio stays bounded,\n`κ(t) = O(1)`.  Carried as a hypothesis from the conjectural\ncone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.core_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.core_bound","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/root-of-unity-truncation.lean#L55-L55","doc":"**Bounded-degree core bound.**  At a root of unity the core\nboundary is a trigonometric polynomial of degree `≤ (κ-1)/2`,\nso by Bernstein the aspect ratio obeys\n`κ(t) ≤ 1 + C·(κ-1)` for `t < T*` (the hard finite-rank cutoff,\nnot the soft generic damping). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.coreBounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.coreBounded","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/root-of-unity-truncation.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Proposition \"the core aspect ratio stays bounded, `κ(t) = O(1)`\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.nsBlowsUp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.nsBlowsUp","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/root-of-unity-truncation.lean#L47-L47","doc":"Proposition \"NS blows up at the collision\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.coreAspect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.coreAspect","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/root-of-unity-truncation.lean#L45-L45","doc":"Vortex-core aspect ratio `κ(t) = a_⊥/a_∥`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.truncationLevel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.truncationLevel","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/root-of-unity-truncation.lean#L43-L43","doc":"Root-of-unity truncation level `κ` (`q = e^{iπ/κ}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.C","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/root-of-unity-truncation.lean#L41-L41","doc":"Universal Bernstein constant `C > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.tStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.tStar","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/root-of-unity-truncation.lean#L39-L39","doc":"Collision time `T*`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/root-of-unity-truncation.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext","kind":"class","line":12,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/root-of-unity-truncation.lean#L12-L61","doc":"**Conditional hypotheses for the root-of-unity truncation.**\n\nThe proposition is conditional on the q-NS conjecture cone\n(`conj:q-aubin-lions`, `conj:ns-counterexample`,\n`conj:critical-exponent`, `prop:blowup-yekutieli`,\n`conj:regularity-breakdown`) and on the `q`-Laplacian spectral\ntower truncation (`prop:q-laplacian-spectral-tower`).  Rather than\nconcluding the vacuous `True`, this class carries the analytic\nfacts the proposition actually asserts as **explicit\nhypotheses**, and `root_of_unity_truncation_conditional`\n*derives* their conjunction (§3b-cond non-degenerate conditional\npattern, the `q_bkm_criterion` exemplar).\n\nThe fields abstract: `coreAspect t` is the vortex-core aspect\nratio `κ(t) = a_⊥/a_∥`; `truncationLevel` is the root-of-unity\ncutoff `κ` (number of active vortex modes `(κ-1)/2`); `C` the\nuniversal Bernstein constant; `nsBlowsUp` / `coreBounded` the two\nsides of the boxed equivalence.\n\n**2026-11-15 (owner decision, PR #7747, bean `qou-fm7s`).** The field\n`leviNonDegenerate` (\"the Levi form stays non-degenerate at\ncollision\") is replaced by `coreBounded` (\"`κ(t) = O(1)`\"). The Levi\nreading is withdrawn: in dimension 3 the Levi datum is the single\nscalar `ξ·curl ξ` (`prop:core-levi-form`), and branch (A) of\n`conj:levi-degeneracy` is refuted by a Beltrami solution. ","signatureChunk":0}]}